                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238697872",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197990436511",
                            "num_reviews": 315,
                            "playtime_forever": 689,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 689,
                            "playtime_at_review": 689,
                            "last_played": 1793107671
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I'm a massive fan of Disciples.  I have physical copies of Disciples 2 so I went in to this with that mindset.  The Writing is truly awful, the mechanics feel clunky and for some reason there isn't an option to skip incredibly lengthy magic castings?   That would've been a QoL i'd have loved to see. I might have even paid a couple of £'s to buy that option.   However the setting is wonderful, the plot whilst clunky and poorly written IS still valid and something that I like from the Disciples Franchise so this is a toughie, do I recommend it?   .... Yes and No.\n\nI'd suggest you all go play Disciples II and live your life, Disciples III should be an improvement but it's not.",
